d for you even when there is little  or no evidence to confirm that this is  true  special k has a health halo as it's long  been marketed  as a diet friendly option probably  because it's relatively low in calories  and fat free but if we compare the  labels of  special k red berries to let's say a  stereotypical  sugar packed cereal like cinnamon toast  crunch  you can see that they're really not that  different  there's nothing wrong with either of  these cereals so choose whichever one  that you actually  like and it is very possible that  beatrice just loves  special k i like it too but if you're  choosing the diet cereal thinking that  it's  a healthier choice which then just  stimulates the scarcity mentality that  results in a binge it's probably better  to just  have a bowl of cinnamon toast crunch and  call it a day  and on that note let's break down the  stats and  trigger warning i am about to talk  numbers so  feel free to skip ahead to the time  stamp on the screen  if that may be triggering to you so  according to  beatrice's own calorie counting her  nutrition for the day came out to be  about  1543 calories with 31  coming from protein and fat and 38  coming from  carbs she is a little bit low in vitamin  e  d calcium and omega-3 fats but otherwise  she's meeting most of her other  micronutrient needs  i did notice that she takes some of  these as supplements in  another video so i'm happy to hear that  she's got that going on as well  but let's switch gears and discuss what  i really like here  one part of beatrice's videos that  really makes me happy  is her disclaimers where she's talking  about something that maybe is out of her  field of expertise  for example in one of her videos  beatrice is diving into her supplement  routine where she's discussing how  taking fish oil and vitamin d has really  helped to  improve her mood and mental health while  i'm of course glad that those  supplements are  working for her what i love most here is  that s